{"kind":"request","text":"State refactor S1: one lifecycle owner per hosted MCP transport generation\n\nFrom the implicit-state shortlist in a99e32d9 (audit at e50d9eeb; no source drift to main bf6ffe61). In packages/mcp/src/http.ts, a transport's opening, expiry, retirement, persisted-session writes and stream replacement are split across the closed and discarded flags, the lifetime generation, timers, the closing promise and the open and pending stream sets (http.ts:113-129). packages/mcp/src/oauth-http.ts:6 and the hosted service opening in packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:491 hold more of the same lifetime. An error there could revive a retired session or keep access past its deadline.\n\nIn one head:\n1. Give each transport generation one owner that holds its state and is the only code that changes it: opening, open, closing, closed. Make graceful close, detach and abrupt discard three named transitions of that owner.\n2. Move stream-slot ownership and the persisted-session write chain under that owner, so a late write or a late stream after retirement has exactly one place to be refused.\n3. Reconcile oauth-http.ts and the hosted opening with the same owner, or say with a reason why one stays separate.\n\nKeep every current guarantee: a retired session never comes back, a late opening is disposed, access ends at its deadline, the bearer's transport epoch still retires old transports, and an idle transport still closes (http-idle.test.ts). Use the existing witnesses in packages/mcp/test (http, http-idle, hosted*, oauth-*). Add a characterization test only for a guarantee no current test pins, and name it. No new state-machine framework or library, and no wire or protocol change.\n\nRun the changed tests while you work and npm run gate once before review. No deploy: the planner deploys all Workers after landing, keeping hosted MCP closed, and redeploys dap-connect closed. The O4 live window does not wait for this head; if the browser returns first, O4 runs on the code then on main. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main where each hosted MCP transport generation has a single lifecycle owner with explicit close, detach and discard; every listed guarantee keeps a named witness; changed tests plus one gate before review; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"bf6ffe617fb1ac6f0e14c39a6f1f93534182bc31","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}